-- 023 — bank holidays beyond 2026.
--
-- bank_holidays held eight rows, 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-28, and nothing after.
-- pay_load_bank_holidays() returns what it finds, so from 2027-01-01 every bank
-- holiday would silently have paid flat rate instead of the configured 2x
-- multiplier. A money defect with a date on it and nothing watching for it.
--
-- These rows are not typed from memory. They are generated by
-- rg_bank_holidays() in server/pure.php, which is tested in
-- server/tests/run.php against the eight 2026 rows this table already held --
-- it reproduces them exactly, substitute days included -- and against the
-- published 2027 dates and the 2022 Christmas-on-a-Sunday case.
--
-- England and Wales only, which is what the previous rows were. The table stays
-- the source of truth rather than the function: one-off holidays happen, the
-- 2022 Jubilee and the 2023 Coronation among them, and those are inserted here
-- alongside these. Scotland and Northern Ireland differ; if the business ever
-- operates there this table needs a nation column before it needs more rows.

